"""Hastings: Senlac Hill, 14 October 1066.  A sample game for the
Grognard engine.

Harold Godwinson, king of the English for nine months, has beaten the
king of Norway at Stamford Bridge and marched his army the length of
England to meet the next invader.  William, duke of Normandy, has
landed at Pevensey and is burning the country round Hastings.  On a
ridge across the road to London, Harold forms his army in a wall of
shields, and William must break it before night.  Play either side
against the computer, or against a friend at the same screen.

Run it with ./hastings (Python 3 with Tk, nothing else).  The game is
saved to ~/.hastings.json.  ./hastings --selftest checks the map and
plays a game between two computer players.
"""

